{
  "capture": "telemetry/mg90-b__dev-v006-2A-D/bemf-coast/capture-1",
  "notes": "read from the bemf-coast dataset and result, no capture of its own. The no-load current is bemf-coast's i_spin_a, the spin window's last 200 ms through current-scale with its in-drive offset, and i_spin_open_zero_a beside it; the speed is bemf-coast's count of the spin's current ripple. drive_drag_by_level is a + b ln(w / w_ref) fitted per level, valid over its speed range. The coast's speed is counted in windows of whole ripple cycles down every coast, no Ke involved; coast_decel_late_rad_s2 is a + b sqrt(w) through the decelerations more than 60 ms past the cut. alpha at the cut is a parabola in time through the ripple's crossings over the stretch where the speed falls 30 %, the speed at the cut pinned to the spin's count. j_kg_m2 is the spin-up route, the median of Kt (I - I0(w)) over the acceleration in the spin-up's windows with 150 mA and more over the settled curve of the level, both levels and directions; its bounds run from the lowest line route, which lets a torque-free current in the drive show, to the ratio at the cut at the slowest 5.0 V rung, which needs none, since the data does not say which reading is right; j_by_route carries each route; drive_excess_a_by_level is the intercept of Kt I0 on alpha at the cut with one J for both levels, current the spin draws that the coast's deceleration does not account for; spinup_excess_a is the spin-up line's intercept. Added with bemf-coast's meter run: reading_term_a_per_v is bemf-coast's, the crest sample over a DMM in series per volt of the terminal difference at the crest sample; i0_meter_by_speed, drive_drag_by_level_meter, level_gap_meter_a, drive_excess_meter_a_by_level and j_by_route_meter are the same reads on bemf-coast's i_spin_meter_a, the spin's current with the term at its duty taken out (bemf-coast's reading_term_by_duty, 4.29 mA/V at 15 to 40 % and smaller at 60 %), the mean current a series meter reads. A later notebook that needs the drag torque, or a current a meter would read, takes drive_drag_by_level_meter; one that subtracts the drag from a crest-sampled board current at the same rail keeps drive_drag_by_level, since the term is in both. The keys without _meter are unchanged, and j_kg_m2 stays the working J",
